{
  "requirement": "List project-relative file paths in the [selected scope](search.md#choosing-a-source-scope).\nOmitting `prefix` lists all visible project files. If more paths remain, follow `next` as shown in\n[Continuing a paged result](#continuing-a-paged-result).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `list_sources.behavior`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the requirement**\n1. List project-relative file paths in the selected scope. The scope is a file prefix, a directory prefix, or the whole project, and it respects visibility rules.\n2. Omitting `prefix` lists all visible project files.\n3. If more paths remain, the caller follows `next` as described in \"Continuing a paged result\".\n\n**Test mapping**\n- **File prefix.** `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies` in `agent/project_sources.rs` calls `list_sources` with `prefix: \"source.txt\"`. It asserts the exact result `{\"files\":[\"source.txt\"]}`, while the project also holds `.gitignore` and the ignored `ignored.txt`.\n- **Directory prefix, project-relative paths and visibility.** `supplied_agent_uses_attached_project_tools_in_both_configuration_orders` in `agent/configured.rs` calls `list_sources` with `prefix: \"visible\"` through a real agent loop. The project has `alpha.txt`, `beta.txt` and `unused.txt` outside the prefix, and `visible/ignored.txt` excluded by `.gitignore`. A decoy project is attached in the other order. The test asserts `files == [\"visible/selected.txt\"]`, so out-of-scope files, ignored files and the wrong project are all excluded. It runs in both attach orders.\n- **Omitted prefix.** `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` in `agent/project_sources.rs` calls `list_sources` with `{}`. Together, its pages cover all 200 files. `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` in `agent/tests.rs` checks that omitting the prefix reaches the provider as scope `\"\"`, and that `src/` is forwarded as given. `gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository` in `tests/source_defaults.rs` checks `SourceScope::all()` against `SourceScope::default()`, with and without a git repository. It asserts that:\n  - dotfiles and nested `.gitignore` exceptions are listed;\n  - ignored files, including ones git tracks, are not listed;\n  - `.git/` is not listed;\n  - listing under an ignored path or the ignored `skip` directory returns nothing.\n- **Paging via `next`.** The 200-file test follows `next` with `get_next_page` until it ends and asserts the concatenated `files` equal the expected list in order. A file added after the first page does not appear, so continuations come from the original listing. `source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads` in `agent/tests.rs` also follows `next` for `list_sources` and checks that no dependencies are recorded.\n\n**Scope matching.** Whole-component matching, where `under(\"src\")` excludes `src-old`, belongs to `requirements.sdk.graph.search.source_scope`, which has its own tests. The only test of it that I found is the `search_text` check in the `source_defaults` test. `SourceScope::contains` uses `Path::starts_with` on components and is shared by all operations. I therefore treat this as delegated and not a gap here.\n\nNo acknowledgments (`{fixme}`) apply. I found no gap.",
  "references": "9b598dbede71c61e2c43c9e0f863580c991f6cfd534e580bd5593f70e3d26cfc",
